The sequence of numerators of the convergents of the continued fraction for the square root of 2 is given by the recurrence relation:
\[ a_{n+1} = 2a_n + a_{n-1} \]
with initial conditions \( a_0 = 1 \) and \( a_1 = 1 \). The terms of this sequence are related to the NSW primes when they are prime numbers.

